      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/90cbc1835ebcfb55d127f820a00e6b25d19731e728a0c5f14ebe81cd027a6593.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-coordinate of the point $S?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of $S,$ we start at the origin, move $3$ units *right*, and then $4$ units *down*. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/f66ac048a9d310784baf5803bc0533cec8438c3b77d10a250de539e3861296d7.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $S$ are $(3,-4).$ Therefore, the $y$-coordinate of $S$ is $-4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
