      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/df0d0dc8ce2cbc15cf6b2060f1a402f876c984cc884d70508cc6a55850e28ed3.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-coordinate of the point $R?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of $R,$ we start at the origin, move $3$ units *left*, and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/3e2476fece6e8789c5560a6c16242efa5da955e39317be06823416f9ae9c8661.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $R$ are $(-3,-3).$ Therefore, the $x$-coordinate of $R$ is $-3.$",
