      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/efb51633cb6a4bc68d0a7c78ec435cd6a11ce87073e3eb704720c09d75b8b488.png)\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $B?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point $B,$ we start at the origin, move $3$ unit *left* and then $1$ unit *down*. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/be37259f84b49b4ad87e19f8908b7992e9d89e3f51fe96ac36edb5f7220fc694.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of $B$ is $-3,$ the $y$-coordinate is $-1,$ and coordinates are given by the ordered pair $(-3,-1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
