    "q-5748": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5748",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/130150cf591ee147d98cc2c265ce1c4790d9570af2b99c0c31d66d9cb7df9b4f.png)\n\nWhat are the $xy$-coordinates of the point shown in the axes above?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point, we inspect its position along the $x$ and $y$ axes.\n\nThe point lies *on* the $y$-axis, $9$ units *below* the origin in the *negative* direction of the $y$-axis. So, the point has an $x$-coordinate of $0,$ and a $y$-coordinate of $-9.$\n\nTherefore, its coordinates are $(0,-9).$",
