    "q-61349": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61349",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/098579a792cd5fe253661082b3cc0a909c68e21a7b6ab11eae4f5a0644cb1195.png)\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $A?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coordinates of the point $A,$ we start at the origin, move $2$ unit *left* and then $3$ units *down*. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/28f80206ef851fe3228ca616beb78f5df28d8d1c866cc77f8042af2c8b72e779.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $-2,$ the $y$-coordinate is $-3,$ and coordinates are given by the ordered pair $(-2,-3).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-61349-a",
