    "q-22344": {
      "dom_id": "step-q22344",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Which of the following shows the point $C(-2,-3)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units to the *left*, in the negative direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-3,$ so we move $3$ units *down*, in the negative direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/2b5ecad03de381cb38267d7d7d72b55465e0888968b8c3e51c4c98d2fe67bd5f.png)",
