    "q-22349": {
      "dom_id": "step-q22349",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Which of the following shows the point $A(-3,4)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $A.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $A$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3,$ so we move $3$ units to the *left*, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $A$ has a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units *up*, in the *positive* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/8d01de8e9083927004153c69fb94407acd6f5e0fbad7b5cf1e9e06198994933d.png)",
